  "notes": "The payload is the single LedgerCloseMeta cut from the data lake's LedgerCloseMetaBatch (the 12-byte batch header removed). The signer's ed25519 key is the source account's own key, so the P… and G… strkeys share a prefix. Both verdicts were measured on 2026-11-17 by replaying this payload into the wallet-backend ingest binary built at each ref (repro/README.md): the pre-fix binary fails five persist attempts and exits with the cursor at 4437356; the post-fix binary ingests the ledger and stores the 41-byte signer key. The #716 verdicts were measured the same day: at 79ea2acd1dc6, the commit the issue was filed against, the ledger is ingested and the signer is stored as 33 bytes (the P version byte and the ed25519 key; length and payload dropped), a row that reads back as a strkey that does not decode. Only the signed-payload producer of #716 is covered by this entry."
